
1. Update Kali Linux
1.	Open a terminal in Kali.[geeksforgeeks]
2.	Run:
bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt -y full-upgrade
This updates packages before installing the web stack.[geeksforgeeks]
 
2. Install Apache, MariaDB, and PHP
1.	In the terminal, install the required services and PHP modules:
bash
sudo apt install apache2 mariadb-server php php-mysqli php-gd libapache2-mod-php -y
Apache provides the web server; MariaDB provides the database; PHP and modules are required for DVWA.[geeksforgeeks]
2.	Enable and start services:
bash
sudo systemctl enable apache2 mariadb
sudo systemctl start apache2 mariadb
This ensures the web server and database start now and on boot.[tecnosender]
 
3. Download DVWA into the Web Root
1.	Change to the Apache web root directory:
bash
cd /var/www/html
DVWA must reside under the web root to be served by Apache.[geeksforgeeks]
2.	Install Git if needed, then clone DVWA:
bash
sudo apt install git -y
sudo git clone https://github.com/digininja/DVWA.git
This downloads the DVWA source code into /var/www/html/DVWA.[geeksforgeeks]
 
4. Set DVWA Directory Permissions
1.	Verify the DVWA directory exists:
bash
ls
You should see DVWA listed.[geeksforgeeks]
2.	Set broad permissions so the web server can read and write files for lab use:
bash
sudo chmod -R 777 DVWA
The video uses chmod -R 777; in a real environment you would prefer tighter www-data ownership, but for a local test lab this is acceptable.[youtube][geeksforgeeks]
 
5. Prepare the DVWA Configuration File
1.	Change into the DVWA configuration directory:
bash
cd DVWA/config
[geeksforgeeks]
2.	Copy the default configuration template:
bash
sudo cp config.inc.php.dist config.inc.php
DVWA uses config.inc.php as the active configuration file.[geeksforgeeks]
3.	Open config.inc.php in a text editor:
bash
sudo mousepad config.inc.php
(Any editor such as nano or vim is acceptable; the video uses a GUI editor.)[geeksforgeeks]
4.	Set database credentials in the file, for example:
o	Database user: admin
o	Database password: password
Update the corresponding lines in config.inc.php, then save and close.[geeksforgeeks]
 
6. Create the DVWA Database and User
1.	Start a MariaDB shell as root:
bash
sudo mysql -u root -p
Leave the password blank and press Enter if no root password is configured.[youtube][geeksforgeeks]
2.	Create the DVWA database:
sql
CREATE DATABASE dvwa;
[geeksforgeeks]
3.	Create a dedicated DVWA user and grant privileges, matching the credentials you set in config.inc.php (example: admin / password):
sql
CREATE USER 'admin'@'127.0.0.1' IDENTIFIED BY 'password';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON dvwa.* TO 'admin'@'127.0.0.1';
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
EXIT;
This allows DVWA to connect to the dvwa database from localhost using the specified user.[youtube][geeksforgeeks]
 
7. Adjust PHP Configuration (allow_url_include)
1.	Locate the PHP configuration file under Apache’s configuration directory (for example, /etc/php/8.2/apache2/php.ini, version may differ).[youtube][geeksforgeeks]
2.	Change to the directory and edit php.ini:
bash
cd /etc/php/8.2/apache2
sudo mousepad php.ini
Replace 8.2 with your installed PHP version if needed.[youtube][digininja-dvwa.mintlify]
3.	Use the editor’s search function to find allow_url_fopen and allow_url_include.[youtube]
4.	Ensure both directives are set to On:
text
allow_url_fopen = On
allow_url_include = On
DVWA requires allow_url_include for some vulnerabilities to function; the video explicitly enables these flags.[geeksforgeeks][youtube]
5.	Save changes and close the editor.[youtube]
 
8. Restart Apache
1.	Restart Apache to apply the PHP configuration changes:
bash
sudo systemctl restart apache2
[geeksforgeeks][youtube]
 
9. Access DVWA in the Browser
1.	Open a web browser inside Kali (for example, Firefox).[geeksforgeeks]
2.	Navigate to:
text
http://127.0.0.1/DVWA
This should load the DVWA login/setup page.[youtube][geeksforgeeks]
3.	If you see a warning about missing database tables, click the Setup or Create / Reset Database button in the DVWA interface to initialise the schema.[digininja-dvwa.mintlify]
 
10. Log In and Verify
1.	On the DVWA login page, use the default credentials:
o	Username: admin
o	Password: password
[digininja-dvwa.mintlify]
2.	After logging in, confirm that DVWA loads the main interface and that modules (such as SQL Injection or XSS) are available.[geeksforgeeks]
3.	Optionally set DVWA Security to Low to begin testing, then raise the level as needed for your experiments.[digininja-dvwa.mintlify]

